[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781448908","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2781448908","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2781448908,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lyYrM","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T14:22:59Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T14:23:49Z","body":"Tested on a project that uses baked directional lights. When reimporting the lightmap texture as lossless (from VRAM Compressed) the following error comes up. \r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n   at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\nERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n   at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\nERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n   at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\nERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n   at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe lossless texture works fine as `RGBAHalf`. I assume it is intended for the error messages to show?\r\n[BakedDirectional.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19621812/BakedDirectional.zip)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781448908/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781490713","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2781490713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2781490713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lyi4Z","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T16:02:54Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T16:02:54Z","body":"> Tested on a project that uses baked directional lights. When reimporting the lightmap texture as lossless (from VRAM Compressed) the following error comes up.\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n>    at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\n> ERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n>    at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\n> ERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n>    at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\n> ERROR: Image format RGBHalf not supported by hardware, converting to RGBAHalf.\r\n>    at: _validate_texture_format (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:2275)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> The lossless texture works fine as `RGBAHalf`. I assume it is intended for the error messages to show? [BakedDirectional.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19621812/BakedDirectional.zip)\r\n\r\nIt's intended, 3-channel texture formats are not supported natively by most GPUs. Though this error will display too often now, it would likely be better for the errors to be converted to warnings and perhaps only show up when using the verbose mode.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781490713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781511284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2781511284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2781511284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lyn50","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T16:56:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T16:56:53Z","body":"The output is now printed as a warning, since an error usually means that a function has ended prematurely (which isn't the case here). It's also only enabled when launching with the `--verbose` flag, since this information is meant for more advanced users","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781511284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781515281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2781515281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2781515281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lyo4R","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T17:07:27Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T17:07:27Z","body":"Hm. Can you do the verbose thing only for the warning that's expected to come up a lot (lightmap texture), while leaving the rest untouched? This would help a lot of people who have \"uh this image does not show up\" problems (quite often it turns out their hardware and/or driver is at fault)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781515281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781518090","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2781518090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2781518090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lypkK","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T17:15:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T17:15:00Z","body":"> Hm. Can you do the verbose thing only for the warning that's expected to come up a lot (lightmap texture), while leaving the rest untouched? This would help a lot of people who have \"uh this image does not show up\" problems (quite often it turns out their hardware and/or driver is at fault)\r\n\r\nI guess I could make an exception for RGB textures, since they're not really expected to be supported on RD backends.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781518090/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791975970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2791975970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2791975970,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6maiwi","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T08:30:15Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T08:30:15Z","body":"> Code looks good to me.\r\n> \r\n> I have some concerns about these messages showing up and looking scary when they are mostly harmless in practice though. The RGB warnings not appearing unless `--verbose` is used should _mostly_ care of this, but still.\r\n\r\nThe more I think about it, maybe the best approach would be to just make the warnings verbose-exclusive? The engine is supposed to decompress unsupported textures by default, the functionality provided by this PR is more so meant for advanced users/engine developers to simplify debugging","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2791975970/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810009360","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104480#issuecomment-2810009360","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104480","id":2810009360,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nfVcQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T15:50:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T15:50:08Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810009360/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]